    "draftContext": {
      "kind": "retained",
      "markdown": "The October 21 acceptance cycle (#416) remains the single blocking item. All four technical blockers have merged fixes as of this window. The next action is a manual trigger of the live provider run against the repaired pipeline; the specific command surface is the acceptance resume workflow introduced in #424. If the provider run fails, the synthetic probe (#428–430) should be run first to isolate schema-side vs. article-fit-side failure before any further code changes are attempted.\n\nPost-token-count for the compacted evidence view (#427) is not yet in the record — it will be produced by the #416 run. The growth rate of evidence as articles accumulate is an open characterization question; #427 is a point fix, not a capacity model.\n\n#421 (October 22 review DRAFT) exits on acceptance of the October 22 action review output, or closes without merge if the pipeline marks it resolved with no material findings.\n\nmorning-cockpit #60 has no activity across two windows and no stated dependency. Its disposition — merge, close, or park — is an owner gate with no technical blocker.\n\nlego-village-pipeline #44, #45, #46 are analysis-only DRAFTs with no active blockers identified. Closing them vs. converting to issues is an owner decision; they are accumulating drift at 12+ days open.\n\nclassic-space-venue #4 is parallel work, not a dependency of the editorial pipeline. Its core issue dependencies (#544, #564–567) are wayfinder/world-building research; none are editorial-pipeline blockers.\n\nAPI spend per failed acceptance cycle (~193K input tokens) is not published in this record. That cost dimension would make the compaction fix legible to anyone outside the immediate codebase.\n\nThe `DRAFT_CONTINUATION_CONTEXT` HTML comment block in the raw draft source is machine-readable pipeline state metadata. It is not reader-facing content and should not appear in any published form. Whether it is suppressed at render time or stripped before publication is a pipeline hygiene question for the next hardening pass.\n\n### Coordinator qualification — 2026-10-27\n\nThe preceding draft context is retained verbatim as historical generated material, not as current instructions or verified action dispositions. Current primary sources are https://github.com/ojfbot/daily-logger/pull/416, https://github.com/ojfbot/daily-logger/pull/431, https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/pull/60 and https://github.com/ojfbot/morning-cockpit/issues/57.\n\nOctober21 acceptance PR daily-logger#416 merged on October24 with article Accepted and all three actions still held; this was not a healthy independent action verdict. A merged PR is not an available resume target. daily-logger#431 recorded five isolated empty-output diagnostic passes and the combined-form schema_complexity failure before this article was generated. That diagnostic did not qualify a native article review or verifier and grants no retry authority. The original candidate command strings remain audit custody; no executable capability is inferred from them.\n\nmorning-cockpit#60 remains an open documentation PR, created within the prior reporting window. Its disposition belongs to its owner. morning-cockpit#57 remains an open contract/identity decision with provenance, owner-acceptance and REST/GraphQL parity gates. No merge, closure, readiness, execution or settlement authority follows from this editorial preparation. classic-space-venue#4 and lego-village-pipeline#44 are retained parallel research/draft background for these three candidates; this classification neither resolves their work nor changes their owner gates.\n\nThis supervised source/data refresh prepares one separately authorized native action-review attempt. It does not predict its outcome, dispose of any original candidate, or authorize a probe, extra paid retry or hosted raw-evidence retention."
